# The app image's build context is this folder, the repository root, and not
# app/ (ADR 0012): the two guides the app serves live in docs/, and a build
# can only copy what is inside its context.
#
# On a server this folder is the Install home, which holds the office's .env,
# its secrets, its certificate and its CA root. None of them is ever copied
# into the image, but everything in the context is sent to the Docker daemon
# unless it is named here, so they are named here first. The WhisperX
# service's build has its own context and its own ignore file.

.env
secrets/
tls/
ca/
whisperx-service/

.git/
.github/
caddy/
docs/spec/
docs/research/
docs/adr/

app/tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
